# Test: OSPFv2 NSSA internal-router default route through the operator's read path
# (RFC 3101 Section 2.4, spec-ospf-rfc3101-nssa-defaults AC-10).
#
# VALIDATES: an operator sets `nssa { default-originate true }` on a single-area NSSA
# router. `show ospf database nssa-external` reports the default when the interface
# carries a usable forwarding address, and reports nothing when it does not, which is
# what RFC 3101 Section 2.4 requires of the P-set LSA that leaf asks for.
# PREVENTS: an absence assertion with no control. The run with a usable address is what
# tells "the forwarding-address rule fired" apart from "this router originates nothing".

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf -run TestOSPFNSSAInternalDefaultFunctional -count=1:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=PASS
